{%- doc -%}
  Renders one slide of the collection grid, when it belongs at the current product position.

  Two kinds of section block:
    - `editorial_slide`: a photo with text (sticky, full height, formats...), placed by row / column, as always.
    - `mosaic_slide`: a tile of the mosaic that lives INSIDE the product grid, like on Miu Miu's collection pages:
      a photo or colour panel with a tag, title, text and "Shop" link. It is a cell of the grid (1 to 6 columns by
      1 to 4 rows of the shape chosen in the section), so it lines up with the product cards; the products flow
      around it. It looks like the "Mosaico de slides" section (same tile snippet and CSS).

  Where an editorial slide's values come from (first one that has a value wins):
    - content (image, heading, text, button label, link): the metaobject entry, then the section block;
    - layout (row/column start and span, horizontal position): the metaobject entry, then the section block
      for this slot, then a default;
    - sticky, full height, aspect ratio and mobile padding: the section block (default: off / natural).
    - focal point (which part of the photo stays in view when the slide's frame crops it): the section block, one for the
      desktop photo and one for the mobile photo.
  A mosaic slide takes everything from its block (it has no metaobject entry).

  The metaobject is an entry of the collection metafield `custom.editorial_slides` (type `editorial_slide`).
  Fields it can have: image, image_mobile, heading, text, button_label, link, and optionally row_start,
  row_span, column_span, horizontal_position ("left", "right" or "custom" with column_start).
  A field that the metaobject does not define, or leaves empty, is simply skipped.

  WHICH COLLECTIONS: the section block can list the collections it is for (`show_in_collections`, empty = all of them).
  Without an entry, a block that is not for the current collection draws nothing. With an entry, a block that is not
  for the current collection is ignored (the entry gets the default layout, and takes nothing from that block).

  @param {object} [entry] - The metaobject entry. Blank when the slide comes only from a section block.
  @param {object} [block] - The section block: layout for this slot and fallback content (also what the theme editor selects).
  @param {number} slot_index - Position of this slide in its list (0-based). Used to place a slide that has no layout of its own.
  @param {number} columns - Number of desktop columns of the grid.
  @param {string} [columns_mobile] - Number of columns of the grid on phones ("1" or "2").
  @param {number} global_product_index - Index of the product the loop is on, counted across all pages already loaded.
  @param {number} current_page - The page of products being rendered.
  @param {number} [photo_ratio] - Height / width of a product card's photo (1.25 = 4:5). Used to size the photos of the slides.
  @param {number} [tile_ratio] - Height / width of one cell of a mosaic slide (1.5 = 2:3). A mosaic slide can have its own shape instead (`aspect_ratio` of its block: square, 4:5...): then its height is its width x that shape, whatever its rows.
  @param {string} [fallback_label] - Accessible name for a slide that has no title (the collection's title).
  @param {boolean} [show_entry_text] - Whether the entry's heading, text and button label are shown. When off, only its
    image (and link and layout) is used, so text that has not been reviewed yet is not published.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign columns = columns | plus: 0
  assign columns_mobile_n = columns_mobile | default: 2 | plus: 0
  assign photo_ratio_n = photo_ratio | default: 1.25 | plus: 0.0
  assign tile_ratio_n = tile_ratio | default: 1.5 | plus: 0.0

  # ---- is this block for the collection being shown? ----
  assign block_for_here = true

  if block.settings.show_in_collections.size > 0
    assign block_for_here = false

    for block_collection in block.settings.show_in_collections
      if block_collection.handle == collection.handle
        assign block_for_here = true
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if block_for_here == false
    assign block = nil
  endif

  # ---- layout ----
  assign row_span = entry.row_span.value | default: block.settings.row_span | default: 2 | plus: 0
  assign column_span = entry.column_span.value | default: block.settings.column_span | default: 2 | plus: 0
  assign row_start = entry.row_start.value | default: block.settings.row_start

  if row_start == blank
    # No layout given anywhere: one slide every 6 rows, starting on row 2
    assign row_start = slot_index | times: 6 | plus: 2
  endif

  assign row_start = row_start | plus: 0 | at_least: 1
  assign row_span = row_span | at_least: 1

  # A slide can not be wider than the grid: a wider one would add a column to the whole grid, and one placed
  # on the right would start before the first column (an invalid grid line, so it collapses to one column).
  assign column_span = column_span | at_least: 1 | at_most: columns
  assign column_start_max = columns | minus: column_span | plus: 1

  assign horizontal_position = entry.horizontal_position.value | default: block.settings.horizontal_position | default: 'left' | downcase

  case horizontal_position
    when 'right'
      assign column_start = column_start_max
    when 'custom'
      assign column_start = entry.column_start.value | default: block.settings.column_start | default: 1 | plus: 0
    else
      assign column_start = 1
  endcase

  assign column_start = column_start | at_least: 1 | at_most: column_start_max

  # ---- mosaic slide: what it is and where it shows ----
  assign is_mosaic_slide = false
  assign slide_visible = true
  assign mobile_span = 1

  if block.type == 'mosaic_slide'
    assign is_mosaic_slide = true

    # A start column of its own wins. Without one, the side: left, right (its last columns touch the right edge
    # whatever its width) or automatic (the first free place of its row, from the left, in list order)
    assign mosaic_column_start = block.settings.column_start | plus: 0
    assign mosaic_side = block.settings.horizontal_position | default: 'auto'

    if mosaic_column_start > 0
      assign column_start = mosaic_column_start | at_most: column_start_max
    elsif mosaic_side == 'left'
      assign column_start = 1
    elsif mosaic_side == 'right'
      assign column_start = column_start_max
    else
      assign column_start = 'auto'
    endif

    # On phones a wide slide takes the row (when the grid has 2 columns), a one-column slide takes one cell
    if column_span > 1 and columns_mobile_n > 1
      assign mobile_span = 2
    endif

    # Nothing to show (no photo, colour, tag, title or text): only the theme editor draws it
    if block.settings.image == blank and block.settings.background_color == blank and block.settings.label == blank and block.settings.heading == blank and block.settings.text == blank and request.design_mode != true
      assign slide_visible = false
    endif
  endif

  # Slides are inserted before the product at this position (a row is `columns` products)
  assign slide_position = row_start | minus: 1 | times: columns

  # A block for other collections is not a slide here (with an entry, the entry is the slide)
  if block_for_here == false and entry == blank
    assign slide_visible = false
  endif
-%}

{%- if global_product_index == slide_position and slide_visible -%}
  {%- liquid
    # ---- content ----
    assign image = entry.image.value | default: block.settings.image
    assign image_mobile = entry.image_mobile.value | default: block.settings.image_mobile
    assign link = entry.link.value | default: block.settings.link

    if entry != blank and show_entry_text != true
      assign heading = block.settings.heading
      assign text = block.settings.text
      assign button_label = block.settings.button_label
    else
      assign heading = entry.heading.value | default: block.settings.heading
      assign text = entry.text.value | default: block.settings.text
      assign button_label = entry.button_label.value | default: block.settings.button_label
    endif

    assign accessible_name = heading | strip_html | strip | default: button_label | default: image.alt | default: fallback_label

    # A button that goes nowhere would only look clickable: it is shown only when the slide has a link
    if link == blank
      assign button_label = blank
    endif

    # ---- focal point (from the section block) ----
    assign focal_desktop = 'center'
    assign focal_mobile = 'center'

    if is_mosaic_slide != true
      assign focal_desktop_mode = block.settings.focal_point | default: 'image_presentation'
      assign focal_mobile_mode = block.settings.mobile_focal_point | default: 'image_presentation'
      # On phones the desktop photo is what shows when the slide has no mobile one
      assign focal_mobile_image = image_mobile | default: image

      capture focal_desktop
        render 'liorme-focal-position', mode: focal_desktop_mode, image: image, x: block.settings.focal_x, y: block.settings.focal_y
      endcapture

      capture focal_mobile
        render 'liorme-focal-position', mode: focal_mobile_mode, image: focal_mobile_image, x: block.settings.mobile_focal_x, y: block.settings.mobile_focal_y
      endcapture
    endif

    # ---- behaviour (from the section block) ----
    assign is_sticky = false
    assign is_full_height = false
    assign has_mobile_padding = false
    assign aspect_ratio = 'natural'

    if block.settings.enable_sticky == true
      assign is_sticky = true
    endif

    if block.settings.enable_full_height == true
      assign is_full_height = true
    endif

    if block.settings.enable_mobile_padding == true
      assign has_mobile_padding = true
    endif

    if block.settings.aspect_ratio != blank
      assign aspect_ratio = block.settings.aspect_ratio
    endif

    # The image is above the fold when the slide starts near the top of the first page
    assign image_loading = 'lazy'

    if current_page == 1 and row_start <= 3
      assign image_loading = 'eager'
    endif

    assign width_vw = column_span | times: 100.0 | divided_by: columns

    # Sharpness. The photo fills the slide (object-fit: cover), so it is scaled by whichever side needs more: the
    # file has to be as wide as the slide AND as wide as the slide's HEIGHT x the photo's aspect ratio (a landscape
    # photo in a tall slide is scaled by its height; 'sizes' by width alone made the browser fetch a file half the
    # size it needed, and the photo looked soft). The slide's height:
    #   - mosaic slide: rows x the shape of a cell x the width of one column;
    #   - editorial slide with a format: its width / the format's ratio; otherwise rows x (a card's photo, the
    #     column width x the photo ratio, plus ~72px of text under it); on phones 60vh.
    assign box_ratio = 0

    case aspect_ratio
      when 'square'
        assign box_ratio = 1.0
      when 'portrait'
        assign box_ratio = 0.6667
      when 'portrait_alt'
        assign box_ratio = 0.8
      when 'landscape'
        assign box_ratio = 1.5
      when 'landscape_alt'
        assign box_ratio = 1.25
      when 'landscape_wide_alt'
        assign box_ratio = 1.7778
    endcase

    # The width of the slide on phones
    assign size_m_width = '100vw'

    assign mosaic_shape = 0

    if is_mosaic_slide
      assign cell_m_vw = 100.0 | divided_by: columns_mobile_n
      assign width_m_vw = mobile_span | times: cell_m_vw
      assign size_m_width = width_m_vw | append: 'vw'

      if box_ratio > 0
        # The slide has its own shape (square, 4:5...): height = width x shape, whatever its rows
        assign mosaic_shape = 1.0 | divided_by: box_ratio
        assign slide_height_vw = width_vw | times: mosaic_shape
        assign slide_height_m_vw = width_m_vw | times: mosaic_shape
      else
        assign slide_height_vw = row_span | times: tile_ratio_n | times: 100.0 | divided_by: columns
        assign slide_height_m_vw = row_span | times: tile_ratio_n | times: cell_m_vw
      endif

      assign slide_height_expr = slide_height_vw | append: 'vw'
      assign slide_height_expr_m = slide_height_m_vw | append: 'vw'
    elsif box_ratio > 0
      assign slide_height_expr = width_vw | divided_by: box_ratio | append: 'vw'
      assign slide_height_expr_m = '(100vw / ' | append: box_ratio | append: ')'
    else
      assign slide_height_vw = row_span | times: photo_ratio_n | times: 100.0 | divided_by: columns
      assign slide_height_px = row_span | times: 72
      assign slide_height_expr = '(' | append: slide_height_vw | append: 'vw + ' | append: slide_height_px | append: 'px)'
      assign slide_height_expr_m = '60vh'
    endif

    assign image_sizes = '(min-width: 720px) ' | append: width_vw | append: 'vw, ' | append: size_m_width

    if image != blank
      assign image_aspect = image.aspect_ratio | default: 1
      assign size_desktop = 'max(' | append: width_vw | append: 'vw, calc(' | append: slide_height_expr | append: ' * ' | append: image_aspect | append: '))'
      assign size_mobile = 'max(' | append: size_m_width | append: ', calc(' | append: slide_height_expr_m | append: ' * ' | append: image_aspect | append: '))'
      assign image_sizes = '(min-width: 720px) ' | append: size_desktop | append: ', ' | append: size_mobile
    endif

    assign image_mobile_sizes = '100vw'

    if image_mobile
      assign image_mobile_aspect = image_mobile.aspect_ratio | default: 1
      assign image_mobile_sizes = 'max(' | append: size_m_width | append: ', calc(' | append: slide_height_expr_m | append: ' * ' | append: image_mobile_aspect | append: '))'
    endif

    capture image_srcset
      if image != blank
        render 'liorme-srcset', image: image
      endif
    endcapture

    capture image_mobile_srcset
      if image_mobile
        render 'liorme-srcset', image: image_mobile
      endif
    endcapture

    # The desktop image is hidden on mobile (theme CSS); that is only right when there is a mobile image to
    # take its place. Without one, the same image is shown at every width (a slide with no image on mobile
    # was an empty box).
    assign desktop_image_class = 'collection-editorial-slide__image'

    if image_mobile
      assign desktop_image_class = desktop_image_class | append: ' collection-editorial-slide__image--desktop'
    endif

    assign tile_eager = false

    if image_loading == 'eager'
      assign tile_eager = true
    endif
  -%}

  {%- if is_mosaic_slide -%}
    <div
      class="collection-editorial-slide collection-editorial-slide--cell{% if block.settings.no_gap_next %} collection-editorial-slide--eat-next{% if mobile_span > 1 %} collection-editorial-slide--eat-next-row{% endif %}{% endif %}"
      style="
        --editorial-slide-mobile-span: {{ mobile_span }};
        --editorial-slide-column-start: {{ column_start }};
        --editorial-slide-column-span: {{ column_span }};
        --editorial-slide-row-start: {{ row_start }};
        --editorial-slide-row-span: {{ row_span }};
        {%- if mosaic_shape > 0 %}
        --editorial-slide-shape: {{ mosaic_shape }};
        {%- endif %}
      "
      {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
    >
      {%- render 'collection-mosaic-slide',
        column_span: column_span,
        row_span: row_span,
        image: image,
        image_mobile: image_mobile,
        focal_point: block.settings.focal_point,
        focal_x: block.settings.focal_x,
        focal_y: block.settings.focal_y,
        mobile_focal_point: block.settings.mobile_focal_point,
        mobile_focal_x: block.settings.mobile_focal_x,
        mobile_focal_y: block.settings.mobile_focal_y,
        background_color: block.settings.background_color,
        label: block.settings.label,
        label_color: block.settings.label_color,
        heading: heading,
        text: text,
        button_label: button_label,
        link: link,
        text_position: block.settings.text_position,
        text_color: block.settings.text_color,
        cols: columns,
        cols_m: columns_mobile_n,
        ratio: tile_ratio_n,
        eager: tile_eager,
        sizes: image_sizes
      -%}
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div
      class="collection-editorial-slide{% unless has_mobile_padding %} collection-editorial-slide--no-padding-mobile{% endunless %}"
      style="
        --editorial-slide-mobile-span: {{ mobile_span }};
        --editorial-slide-column-start: {{ column_start }};
        --editorial-slide-column-span: {{ column_span }};
        --editorial-slide-row-start: {{ row_start }};
        --editorial-slide-row-span: {{ row_span }};
        --editorial-slide-focal: {{ focal_desktop }};
        --editorial-slide-focal-mobile: {{ focal_mobile }};
      "
      {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
    >
      <div
        class="collection-editorial-slide__sticky"
        data-sticky="{{ is_sticky }}"
        data-full-vh="{{ is_full_height }}"
        data-aspect-ratio="{{ aspect_ratio }}"
      >
        {%- if link != blank -%}
          <a
            href="{{ link }}"
            class="collection-editorial-slide__link"
            aria-label="{{ accessible_name | strip_html | escape }}"
          ></a>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="collection-editorial-slide__media">
          {%- if image -%}
            <img
              src="{{ image | image_url: width: 1000 }}"
              srcset="{{ image_srcset }}"
              sizes="{{ image_sizes }}"
              alt="{{ image.alt | default: heading | escape }}"
              loading="{{ image_loading }}"
              width="{{ image.width }}"
              height="{{ image.height }}"
              class="{{ desktop_image_class }}"
            >
          {%- else -%}
            {{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: desktop_image_class | append: ' placeholder' }}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if image_mobile -%}
            <img
              src="{{ image_mobile | image_url: width: 800 }}"
              srcset="{{ image_mobile_srcset }}"
              sizes="{{ image_mobile_sizes }}"
              alt="{{ image_mobile.alt | default: heading | escape }}"
              loading="lazy"
              width="{{ image_mobile.width }}"
              height="{{ image_mobile.height }}"
              class="collection-editorial-slide__image collection-editorial-slide__image--mobile"
            >
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <div class="collection-editorial-slide__overlay"></div>

        <div class="collection-editorial-slide__text-container">
          {%- if heading != blank -%}
            <h3 class="collection-editorial-slide__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h3>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if text != blank -%}
            <div class="collection-editorial-slide__text">{{ text | escape | newline_to_br }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if button_label != blank -%}
            <span class="collection-editorial-slide__button btn btn--secondary">
              {{- button_label | escape -}}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
